    "created_at": "2016-03-01T08:51:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-01T08:51:56Z",
    "body": "The alternative here is a new DeepStructuredClone abstract operation if we don't like the level of nesting.\n\nIf we ever need deep clone support for IDL-defined objects my idea would be that we change [[Clone]] to return a record of a value and a whether or not it needs to be deep cloned. And then we'd invoke [[DeepClone]] if that returned true (after adding it to memory). We would probably have DeepStructuredClone then to help with the ECMAScript-defined objects.\n\n(I wonder why we call this structured cloning. Could we not just call this CloneWithTransfer and Clone? What is structured about it?)\n",
